From 12848ffc17904b058d95d2faa1c647fe29afebb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:54:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(machine): built-in lathe and mill-turn Z stroke in
 program coordinates

The limit check reads travel bands in program coordinates through the
work offset (#457). lathe.mch (Z -615..0) and millturn.mch (Z -620..0)
stated machine-frame bands, so every move in front of the face
(program Z > 0) - clearance, approach, facing allowance - was out of
stroke and no turning program posted on either built-in. Restate Z as
the full stroke each way (-615..615, -620..620), the convention PR #477
applies to the mills. X stays 0..R: a lathe X is measured from the
spindle centreline, which is the program's own X0.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/lathe_stroke.rs: a face-and-turn job with
clearance in front of the face passes and posts on both built-ins; a
clearance past the stroke still refuses by name and blocks the post.

Fixes #493

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
